## Summary of what the survey actually shows

**Nobody in this set uses `deny_unknown_fields` on a wire type. Zero occurrences across all five codebases.** Casing splits cleanly by lineage: formats derived from a non-Rust spec (OCI, LSP, SARIF, protobuf JSON) are `camelCase`; formats native to Rust tooling (cargo metadata, cargo `--message-format=json`, rustc diagnostics) are `snake_case`. Forward compat is bought with **open enums + `Option`/`#[serde(default)]`**, never with strict parsing.

---

## 1. oci-spec-rs (`containers/oci-spec-rs`, v0.10.0)

Clone: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/containers/oci-spec-rs`

**`deny_unknown_fields`: 0 occurrences in the entire repo** (`grep -rn deny_unknown_fields` → empty).
**`#[non_exhaustive]`: exactly 1**, and it's on a non-serde type (`DigestAlgorithm`).

`rename_all` census (`src/`):
| casing | count | where |
| :-- | :-- | :-- |
| `camelCase` | ~50 | all image + runtime structs |
| `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` | 7 | `LinuxCapability`, `Signal`, `Arch` (seccomp), `distribution/error.rs` |
| `PascalCase` | 1 | `image::Config` (Docker-inherited) |
| `lowercase` | 4 | `LinuxNamespaceType`, `ContainerState`, zos |

`src/image/descriptor.rs:8-11`:
```rust
#[derive(
    Builder, Clone, CopyGetters, Debug, Deserialize, Eq, Getters, Setters, PartialEq, Serialize,
)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
```
That is the *entire* container attribute set. Same at `src/image/manifest.rs:29`, `src/image/index.rs:22`, `src/image/oci_layout.rs:14`, `src/image/artifact.rs:15`.

The one PascalCase exception, `src/image/config.rs:284` — the Docker-legacy `Config` object whose JSON keys are `User`, `Env`, `Cmd`:
```rust
#[serde(rename_all = "PascalCase")]
```
And spec-literal names override the convention rather than bending it (`src/image/config.rs:69,77`):
```rust
#[serde(rename = "os.version", skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
os_version: Option<String>,
#[serde(rename = "os.features", skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
os_features: Option<Vec<String>>,
```

**Enum representation — this is the load-bearing finding.** `MediaType`, `Os`, and `Arch` are *not* derived serde enums. They are hand-written open enums with an `Other(String)` escape hatch and manual `Serialize`/`Deserialize` that round-trip through `String` (`src/image/mod.rs:28-72, 165-182`):
```rust
/// Media types used by OCI image format spec. Values MUST comply with RFC 6838,
/// including the naming requirements in its section 4.2.
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq)]
pub enum MediaType {
    Descriptor,
    LayoutHeader,
    ImageManifest,
    // ...
    /// MediaType not specified by OCI image format.
    Other(String),
}

impl Serialize for MediaType {
    fn serialize<S>(&self, serializer: S) -> Result<S::Ok, S::Error>
    where S: serde::Serializer {
        let media_type = format!("{self}");
        media_type.serialize(serializer)
    }
}

impl<'de> Deserialize<'de> for MediaType {
    fn deserialize<D>(deserializer: D) -> Result<Self, D::Error>
    where D: serde::Deserializer<'de> {
        let media_type = String::deserialize(deserializer)?;
        Ok(media_type.as_str().into())   // infallible; unknown -> Other(..)
    }
}
```
`Os` (`src/image/mod.rs:188`) and `Arch` (`src/image/mod.rs:291`) are identical in shape, each ending in `Other(String)`. **Deserializing an unknown media type / OS / arch cannot fail.**

`DigestAlgorithm` is the only `#[non_exhaustive]`, and it states the rationale explicitly (`src/image/digest.rs:5-25`):
```rust
/// Other digest algorithms may be added
/// in the future, so this structure is marked as non-exhaustive.
#[non_exhaustive]
#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
pub enum DigestAlgorithm {
    Sha256, Sha384, Sha512,
    /// Any other algorithm. Note that it is possible
    /// that other algorithms will be added as enum members.
    Other(Box<str>),
}
```
Note it carries **both** `#[non_exhaustive]` *and* `Other(_)` — belt and braces.

**Documented tri-state rationale** (`src/runtime/features.rs:38-46`):
```rust
/// The list of the recognized hook names, e.g., "createRuntime".
/// "None" means "unknown", not "no support for any hook".
hooks: Option<Vec<String>>,
/// The list of the recognized mount options, e.g., "ro".
/// "None" means "unknown", not "no support for any mount option".
mount_options: Option<Vec<String>>,
```

The upstream spec requirement they're encoding, quoted in their own doc comment at `src/image/manifest.rs:54-58`: *"Implementations storing or copying image manifests MUST NOT error on encountering an artifactType that is unknown to the implementation."*

No README/CONTRIBUTING rationale — the policy lives in doc comments and in the shape of the types.

---

## 2. lsp-types (`gluon-lang/lsp-types`)

**`deny_unknown_fields`: 0. `#[non_exhaustive]`: 0.**
`rename_all` census: **289 × `camelCase`**, 10 × `lowercase`, 2 × `camelCase` combined with `untagged`.
Also: **53 `#[serde(untagged)]`**, **149 `#[serde(flatten)]`**, **179 `skip_serializing_if`** in `src/lib.rs` alone.

Typical container attrs (`src/lib.rs:947-948`) — again, nothing but casing:
```rust
#[derive(Debug, PartialEq, Clone, Deserialize, Serialize, Default)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
pub struct InitializeParams {
    pub process_id: Option<u32>,
    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
    #[deprecated(note = "Use `root_uri` instead when possible")]
    pub root_path: Option<String>,
    #[serde(default)]
    #[deprecated(note = "Use `workspace_folders` instead when possible")]
    pub root_uri: Option<Uri>,
```

**Union types → `#[serde(untagged)]`** (`src/lib.rs:203-208`, `733-738`, `755-759`):
```rust
#[derive(Debug, Eq, Hash, PartialEq, Clone, Deserialize, Serialize)]
#[serde(untagged)]
pub enum NumberOrString { Number(i32), String(String) }

#[serde(untagged)]
pub enum DocumentChanges { Edits(Vec<TextDocumentEdit>), Operations(Vec<DocumentChangeOperation>) }
```

**LSP's integer enums are modeled as open newtypes, not Rust enums** — the crate's whole forward-compat story (`src/lib.rs:1119-1152`):
```rust
/// A symbol kind.
#[derive(Eq, PartialEq, Copy, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize)]
#[serde(transparent)]
pub struct SymbolKind(i32);
lsp_enum! {
impl SymbolKind {
    pub const FILE: SymbolKind = SymbolKind(1);
    pub const MODULE: SymbolKind = SymbolKind(2);
    // ... through TYPE_PARAMETER = 26
}
}
```
An unrecognized `SymbolKind(99)` deserializes fine; the generated `Debug` impl has a `_ => write!(f, "{}({})", stringify!($typ), self.0)` arm (`src/lib.rs:70-79`). Only the *string* `TryFrom<&str>` conversion can error.

The spec rationale is carried verbatim in the doc comment (`src/lib.rs:1154-1166`):
```rust
/// Specific capabilities for the `SymbolKind` in the `workspace/symbol` request.
pub struct SymbolKindCapability {
    /// The symbol kind values the client supports. When this
    /// property exists the client also guarantees that it will
    /// handle values outside its set gracefully and falls back
    /// to a default value when unknown.
    pub value_set: Option<Vec<SymbolKind>>,
}
```

There's also a revealing comment at `src/lib.rs:740-753` — they *wanted* `#[serde(other)]` on an internally-tagged enum for the fallback case and couldn't have it (serde-rs/serde#912), so they fell back to `untagged`:
```rust
