## 3. cargo_metadata (`oli-obk/cargo_metadata`)

**`deny_unknown_fields`: 0. `#[non_exhaustive]`: 25** — on essentially every public wire struct.
`rename_all` census: **only 5 total** — 1 × `kebab-case`, 4 × `lowercase`. **No `rename_all` on any struct.** Fields serialize as Rust `snake_case`, because cargo's JSON *is* snake_case (`package_id`, `manifest_path`, `workspace_members`, `target_directory`).

`src/lib.rs:257-289`:
```rust
#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
#[cfg_attr(feature = "builder", derive(Builder))]
#[non_exhaustive]
#[cfg_attr(feature = "builder", builder(pattern = "owned", setter(into)))]
/// Starting point for metadata returned by `cargo metadata`
pub struct Metadata {
    pub packages: Vec<Package>,
    pub workspace_members: Vec<PackageId>,
    /// This is not available if running with a version of Cargo older than 1.71.
    #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = "WorkspaceDefaultMembers::is_missing")]
    pub workspace_default_members: WorkspaceDefaultMembers,
    ...
}
```

**Newly-added upstream fields get `#[serde(default)]` plus a version note** — this is the forward-compat convention, repeated throughout (`src/messages.rs:210-214`, `src/lib.rs` `NodeDep`):
```rust
    /// The `OUT_DIR` environment variable where this script places its output
    ///
    /// Added in Rust 1.41.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub out_dir: Utf8PathBuf,
```
```rust
    /// The kinds of dependencies.
    ///
    /// This field was added in Rust 1.41.
    #[serde(default)]
    pub dep_kinds: Vec<DepKindInfo>,
```

**Three distinct open-enum idioms, all in one crate:**

`#[serde(other)]` catch-all (`src/dependency.rs:13-29`):
```rust
pub enum DependencyKind {
    #[serde(rename = "normal")] #[default] Normal,
    #[serde(rename = "dev")] Development,
    #[serde(rename = "build")] Build,
    #[doc(hidden)]
    #[serde(other)]
    Unknown,
}
```

`#[serde(untagged)]` string fallback + `#[non_exhaustive]` + a written policy in the doc comment (`src/lib.rs:771-817`):
```rust
/// Kind of target.
/// ...
/// Other possible values may be added in the future.
#[derive(Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, PartialOrd, Ord)]
#[non_exhaustive]
pub enum TargetKind {
    #[serde(rename = "bench")] Bench,
    #[serde(rename = "bin")] Bin,
    #[serde(rename = "custom-build")] CustomBuild,
    ...
    /// Unknown type
    #[serde(untagged)]
    Unknown(String),
}
```

Hand-rolled fallback with *two* unknown arms, and the rationale spelled out (`src/messages.rs:38-56`):
```rust
#[non_exhaustive]
pub enum ArtifactDebuginfo {
    #[default] None, LineDirectivesOnly, LineTablesOnly, Limited, Full,
    /// An unknown integer level.
    ///
    /// This may be produced by a version of rustc in the future that has
    /// additional levels represented by an integer that are not known by this
    /// version of `cargo_metadata`.
    UnknownInt(i64),
    /// An unknown string level.
    ///
    /// This may be produced by a version of rustc in the future that has
    /// additional levels represented by a string that are not known by this
    /// version of `cargo_metadata`.
    UnknownString(String),
}
```

Top-level message dispatch (`src/messages.rs:225-245`):
```rust
#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
#[non_exhaustive]
#[serde(tag = "reason", rename_all = "kebab-case")]
pub enum Message {
    CompilerArtifact(Artifact),
    CompilerMessage(CompilerMessage),
    BuildScriptExecuted(BuildScript),
    /// Added in Rust 1.44.
    BuildFinished(BuildFinished),
    /// A line of text which isn't a cargo or compiler message.
    #[serde(skip)]
    TextLine(String),
}
```
`#[non_exhaustive]` on `Message` is exactly the "an unknown `reason` may appear" hedge — combined with `TextLine(String)` for non-JSON stdout lines.

README and CHANGELOG contain **no** written policy statement about field addition. The policy is encoded structurally: `#[non_exhaustive]` on every struct means adding a public field is not a semver-major change (see §7 citation below).

