## 6. rustc's JSON output — the exact citation you wanted

https://doc.rust-lang.org/rustc/json.html, source at `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rust-lang/rust/master/src/doc/rustc/src/json.md` lines 14-18, verbatim:

> Each type of message has a `$message_type` field which can be used to distinguish the different formats. When parsing, care should be taken to be forwards-compatible with future changes to the format. Optional values may be `null`. New fields may be added. Enumerated fields like "level" or "suggestion_applicability" may add new values.

And line 320:

> Note that the JSON format of the `timings` messages is unstable and subject to change.

Casing of the actual payload is **snake_case** (`json.md:60-80`): `file_name`, `byte_start`, `byte_end`, `line_start`, `line_end`, `suggested_replacement`, `suggestion_applicability`, plus the sigil field `$message_type`. Enumerated values are kebab/lower strings: `"failure-note"`, `"MachineApplicable"` (the applicability one is PascalCase — inconsistent, deliberately open).

