## 8. Bonus data point — serde-sarif (`psastras/sarif-rs`)

A stable, externally-specified JSON format (OASIS SARIF 2.1.0) generated into Rust via `schemafy_lib` from `serde-sarif/src/schema.json`. **`deny_unknown_fields`: 0. `#[non_exhaustive]`: 0. 11 × `rename_all = "camelCase"` on the enums**, e.g. `serde-sarif/src/sarif.rs:21-24`:
```rust
#[doc = "The role or roles played by the artifact in the analysis."]
#[derive(Display, Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, EnumString)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
#[strum(serialize_all = "camelCase")]
pub enum ArtifactRoles { AnalysisTarget, Attachment, ... }
```
The interesting bit: the bundled SARIF schema contains **52 instances of `"additionalProperties": false`** — the format is officially closed — yet the Rust binding does not enforce it. Even a spec that says "closed" gets a deserializer that shrugs at unknown fields.

